body:
@TrySound Using `--no-treeshake` produces the same invalid output.

It does modify the output if I add more code to the base file:

---

**Extra code in the base with tree shaking:**

``` js
// base.js

export class Base {
  foo() {
    return true;
  }
}

Base.static = true;
```

> rollup main.js

``` js
class Thing extends Base {
  bar() {
    return true;
  }
}

export { Thing };
```

> Uncaught ReferenceError: Base is not defined

---

**Extra code in the base without tree shaking:**

``` js
// base.js

export class Base {
  foo() {
    return true;
  }
}

Base.static = true;
```

> rollup --no-treeshake main.js

``` js
Base.static = true;

class Thing extends Base {
  bar() {
    return true;
  }
}

export { Thing };
```

> Uncaught ReferenceError: Base is not defined

Strangely, the class declaration is removed even though tree shaking is disabled, but the other code in the base file is preserved.
